# Keep the build context to the SOURCE only.
#
# Without this file, `docker build ... .` from the repo root uploads the local
# node_modules tree (~2GB of pnpm store symlinks, which also breaks COPY) and
# the .nx cache. Both are regenerated inside the image by `pnpm install`, so
# shipping them is pure cost — and a host node_modules built for a different
# libc/arch than node:22-alpine would actively poison the build.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Compiled output. Dockerfile.build recompiles these from source on purpose:
# leaking a host-built dist/ in would defeat the point of building from a clean
# checkout and could mask a genuinely broken build.
dist
**/dist
tmp
**/tmp
out-tsc

# ...EXCEPT the four dist trees the SIBLING `Dockerfile` COPYs directly.
#
# .dockerignore is per-CONTEXT, not per-Dockerfile, so this one file also
# governs `docker build -f backend/plugins/frontline_api/Dockerfile .` — the
# packaging-only recipe that .github/workflows/ci-api-frontline.yml runs with
# `context: .` AFTER building the two projects on the runner. A blanket
# `**/dist` silently removes its inputs from the context and that build dies
# with the un-Googleable
#   failed to compute cache key: "/backend/erxes-api-shared/dist": not found
# Re-including them costs Dockerfile.build nothing: its own stage-1 `COPY . .`
# lands before `pnpm nx build`, which overwrites these paths anyway, and on a
# clean checkout (Dokploy) they are gitignored and simply absent.
!backend/erxes-api-shared/dist
!backend/erxes-api-shared/utils/dist
!backend/erxes-api-shared/core-types/dist
!backend/erxes-api-shared/core-modules/dist
!backend/plugins/frontline_api/dist

.nx
.git
.github
.agents
.claude
.vscode
.idea

# Docs and local-only artifacts
*.md
!backend/**/*.md
.env
.env.*
!.env.sample
dump.rdb
storybook-static
coverage
**/coverage
.pnpm-store
